      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The curtain has dropped on the Blue Jays' season, and what's left is less chase than cleanup. <strong>Toronto fell 5-1 to the Reds on Saturday</strong>, slipping to 78-83 and fifth in the AL East, a flat ending to a year that never found enough pitching or health to hold together. Max Scherzer gets the finale tonight at Rogers Centre, and the old warrior is suddenly the most interesting man in the building - not for a pennant push, but for whether this is his last ride. Trey Yesavage's brief cameo offered a glimpse of the future, and that matters now. <strong>Watch the finale, then watch the winter: young arms like Yesavage, and a front office that must find real starting pitching</strong>.",
